<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}+4x+3\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"9\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{4}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$16{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$12x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$13{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$12x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$13{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$52x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$39$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$40x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$39$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{4}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4} & =q(x)p(x)+(-40x-39),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{2}-4x+13.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=q(A)p(A)+(-40A-39I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & =q(A)p(A)+(-40A-39I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-40A-39I) \\\\  & =-40A-39I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Inverse of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Its Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad1c106-e555-5ab5-a741-a4cdc7c69178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321234} {:answer/id #uuid "34a01fff-5e6b-50b0-9a81-d354a982151b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321548} {:answer/id #uuid "5c921480-996f-547f-b72f-7f34613e006b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321880} {:answer/id #uuid "80f9676b-bed6-5d2f-bf33-5b0764fda6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322161} {:answer/id #uuid "9dcf1a38-313b-56b9-aaf8-6ce81f6c07cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c921480-996f-547f-b72f-7f34613e006b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321880} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f66c2c3-662d-5a6c-b51b-54dc28c47dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4acccd18-c797-5d41-ab58-67f98662f9b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-37779" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value of $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 1 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-8A+9I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-8A+9I) & =O \\\\ A-8I+9{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{8}{9}I-\\frac{1}{9}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{8}{9},$ $q=-\\frac{1}{9},$ and \n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{8}{9}+(-\\frac{1}{9})=\\frac{7}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124538 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial Using the Cayley-Hamilton Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834aa185-6012-5fad-9cec-bfae8e36cc07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392142} {:answer/id #uuid "ba614c81-25e5-56b2-a980-247e1c339a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392143} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8f194b-9c47-54bc-9f21-95b6a53aec45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392144} {:answer/id #uuid "30a72e6d-1f6b-54c6-a30e-be3b5a7ecb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392145} {:answer/id #uuid "918cb8aa-dfd0-58f5-94c4-133741fe2164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30a72e6d-1f6b-54c6-a30e-be3b5a7ecb69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392145} :answer-field/id #uuid "8edebb12-abdf-545c-97fb-264d8989834b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9892d6a4-00e5-53a4-a283-14b8510646e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37835" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\nand $\\,f(x)={x}^{22}-{x}^{20}+3x-2\\,$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )+8 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{20}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-1\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{22}\\,-\\,{x}^{20}\\,+\\,3x\\,-\\,2\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{22}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{20}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(3x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{20}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(3A-2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(3A-2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(3A-2I) \\\\  & =3A-2I \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum and Product of Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7626ec-5cdf-5183-920c-f615785a0c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123447} {:answer/id #uuid "b4168450-826c-5d6f-87df-97fac24fbe08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123448} {:answer/id #uuid "d3835a1d-1d0e-55ab-b5fd-050dd5742e1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123449} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd25f67-3b58-5e3d-a82e-896e9d4fd2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123450} {:answer/id #uuid "637a2fa6-0b06-55fc-aaf1-13e03d850dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7626ec-5cdf-5183-920c-f615785a0c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123447} :answer-field/id #uuid "3734faa8-d4ad-5237-863b-7669bf2a5f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "686a322b-e1a0-51fa-9c41-edfcff1a5f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-38726" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-14 & -2 \\\\ 71 & 10\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & -2 \\\\ 71 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-14)\\cdot 10-(-2)\\cdot 71 \\\\  & =-140+142 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Inverse of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Its Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "510817f0-e7bd-55d8-aac0-a9a53f33dfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324638} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7e1c61-aa2e-5bf9-a431-0d2a530a4e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324767} {:answer/id #uuid "87078d7e-1d91-58fc-93d9-8ea539d7c748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325122} {:answer/id #uuid "d65c484e-4497-5ea7-969c-2e747c2f286c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325834} {:answer/id #uuid "efa28b9a-8c62-5a82-bbad-05c2a07878f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7e1c61-aa2e-5bf9-a431-0d2a530a4e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324767} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd9dcafd-a586-57d5-a20b-4b6957e12103" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d668f123-34ae-5571-83d2-f3aa0e4c070a" :question/math-academy-id "q-40173" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}],$ and ${A}^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value of $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-5A-2 & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-5A-2) & ={A}^{-1}O \\\\ A-5I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =-\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{5}{2},$ $q=\\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\np+q=-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum and Product of Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111b65d-3f2a-53be-b9c8-72140db0c000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348594} {:answer/id #uuid "21c84e48-2f7a-50e2-ae10-a98b55224ea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348738} {:answer/id #uuid "af812824-ba2d-513e-aafb-b6e3481d2fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349997} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6f7128-5303-5476-a78f-fdc72719a647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350100} {:answer/id #uuid "f87ed33c-0627-5feb-8b51-4691049fc090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f87ed33c-0627-5feb-8b51-4691049fc090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350626} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad93b77f-5c01-5827-a026-411c6805c1cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0a5592f-8700-52f5-9072-d916c7a1624f" :question/math-academy-id "q-83390" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=5-6=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum and Product of Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21bb0307-ef7e-526c-b538-d534a6591d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348737} {:answer/id #uuid "5a33f56a-d343-56b9-9e1a-e2c6c3ef7257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349276} {:answer/id #uuid "7f481017-87d3-5fa9-8268-0a5954b611d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349611} {:answer/id #uuid "ae32a17a-1402-5f65-a95b-a6f83e678ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349985} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b7bbae-96c5-569e-b3c4-02448f16a87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9b7bbae-96c5-569e-b3c4-02448f16a87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350092} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd1f4542-30de-5ffb-aae5-ab11763e48cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "740b80bf-831e-5f73-a545-985d989c4d40" :question/math-academy-id "q-83391" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 7-(-5)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-28+15 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124537 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2867571-c1ae-5ea0-b784-22f444c8db38" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Power of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Smaller Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bde7c58-3f7c-5801-a261-da5680905d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9A+5I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430396} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2122a1-0044-5550-a7b5-8c659f887082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5A+9I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430398} {:answer/id #uuid "8506e219-a01e-50d0-9da2-c59e5aa39951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9A-5I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430399} {:answer/id #uuid "