n theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-14A+36I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum and Product of Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d65a687-0988-5518-994a-fcab04da4ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430395} {:answer/id #uuid "4571d412-17c6-50e3-a5ad-250aba5664ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430397} {:answer/id #uuid "8600afc6-a04f-52fd-8a1f-de56606615bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430400} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2cc7ac-9a1b-526d-80a8-a3d8c973934c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430404} {:answer/id #uuid "f2683b79-0149-589d-9aee-43b4a2b94124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2683b79-0149-589d-9aee-43b4a2b94124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430406} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6843fb7-59e5-5002-ac90-2b5e6f7257b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a565f00-30b9-57be-9036-7aadde82bfe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-85922" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=4-2=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum and Product of Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a38ceb7-78e0-536d-b6f4-5b0d0fb36963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352364} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c95411-022b-5df9-be2d-f24fb668a56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352943} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a3ef71-3f78-5e0f-8cd1-ac73a5157b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353251} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f74d25-1c42-5e42-9c74-52425e6e436f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353305} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ef4f6b-04cb-5b34-8ba0-40661d358f31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2a3ef71-3f78-5e0f-8cd1-ac73a5157b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353251} :answer-field/id #uuid "3028fca6-be53-57d1-86aa-5aa3f7020ab2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d05c0df-0883-5373-84c3-aa2cb3f54a04" :question/math-academy-id "q-85923" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =-15-10 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124537 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2867571-c1ae-5ea0-b784-22f444c8db38" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Power of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Smaller Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c0f630-3d3f-5ed2-b141-b4de74558d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2A-22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351749} {:answer/id #uuid "1c032529-58f9-5c6d-bb8a-28b0d83dcf4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{A}^{2}-22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351819} {:answer/id #uuid "4c54e098-dfe0-5b60-9eda-b99474cc5cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2A+22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352264} {:answer/id #uuid "51747fe9-4344-5df8-a2b3-99b62f01c228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{A}^{2}+22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352299} {:answer/id #uuid "adf1cc36-8df2-5b24-b96f-d8364c7549da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22{A}^{2}+2I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51747fe9-4344-5df8-a2b3-99b62f01c228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{A}^{2}+22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352299} :answer-field/id #uuid "a23b76ae-ab3d-5595-bd99-e08ffc6e5c76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3d8a5b7-428e-5b9f-a099-8d78abc215c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-85926" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix with the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=-{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+22.$ Then, ${A}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{3}+2{A}^{2}+22I & =O \\\\ {A}^{3} & =2{A}^{2}+22I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Inverse of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Its Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb6cd75-1b66-5eef-bdd2-d1c1efa8bd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351849} {:answer/id #uuid "3110eedf-37d2-5058-a8cb-2890631cedaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352019} {:answer/id #uuid "50826028-f314-5a71-8097-5a7dc84cf792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49I-12A+{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352291} {:answer/id #uuid "b3125bf0-b9d9-57a1-9d2f-231388faed3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353099} {:answer/id #uuid "dca93f44-d070-505c-ab70-65f10c6983ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9I+2A+{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3125bf0-b9d9-57a1-9d2f-231388faed3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353099} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec8c9dce-00e3-5b5f-901c-e3b2b9cd794b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cddc84f4-8d27-54c1-a11e-f66ad824ed8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-85929" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +29) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+12{\\lambda }^{2}-49\\lambda +58 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+12A-49I+58{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Inverse of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Its Powers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054199c2-5c89-5ffd-aead-8b50d8e9a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430393} {:answer/id #uuid "10181856-84b4-5e5e-8832-61fff9b19f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A+\\frac{3}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430394} {:answer/id #uuid "87762782-8da5-5b58-aec6-89ebd72a1767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430401} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1bad79-e653-5c1b-8674-be7f593dc2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}I-\\frac{5}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430402} {:answer/id #uuid "97594f4f-bc35-5637-b1b2-7a025224b4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "054199c2-5c89-5ffd-aead-8b50d8e9a898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430393} :answer-field/id #uuid "34db680c-e9af-57f5-a298-893f9c03dc9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f9a6384-39b0-554b-abeb-cd550f81dcbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-85930" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )+2) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+5\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+5A-2I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+5A-2I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+5I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ 2{A}^{-1} & =5I-{A}^{2} \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124538 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial Using the Cayley-Hamilton Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dadc6e-37e2-586e-a762-b4874076a22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20A+21I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351603} {:answer/id #uuid "341e8f60-2c2f-5139-b327-47e278c2e00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20A-21I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352054} {:answer/id #uuid "67808fb2-87cd-5157-a1e0-94315005596d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352488} {:answer/id #uuid "a32d7b40-8537-52c2-946a-2c71554d7a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A-20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352961} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3590d8-8a17-530d-9efd-1e18f0a866be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3590d8-8a17-530d-9efd-1e18f0a866be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353325} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ced7d20-506d-5fe9-bbfe-309a56bbc614" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62f9e5ba-0775-5b99-88ac-c3c5c53cda55" :question/math-academy-id "q-85931" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-x-20\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"9\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$21x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(21x+20),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+1.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =21A+20I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
